<h2 id="what" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. What this is</h2>

**Traffic cop** for live paragraph-gen testing on Place / Number / Other Word
**and Noun gender** admin scopes.

```text
Door A: first 5 pool words ×2  →  both must PASS
Door B: all pool words ×1      →  PASS → shipped (pipeline)
Door C: batched Pair A + Pair B judges (YAML judge_a / judge_b) on Door B texts
        → shipped_and_verified (default on; --no-door-c skips)
```

- **`shipped`** = Door A+B only. **`shipped_and_verified`** = A+B+C.
- Door C snapshots paragraphs **before** harness bulk-delete; one Pair-A call + one Pair-B call over the batch (not per paragraph). Default live pair: Claude + OpenAI. Restore Gemini: set `door_c.judge_a.provider: gemini` (and model) in `main_config.yaml`, or env `DOOR_C_JUDGE_A_PROVIDER=gemini`.
- Modes (YAML `non_conj_paragraph.door_c.mode`): **`ALL_SHIPPED_SCOPES`** (default) or **`PER_SHIPPED_SCOPE`**. Still judges the pipeline-passed subset if another scope failed A/B.
- Dual approve: **both** judges must mark each paragraph `OK` to pass Door C; **any** `ISSUE` fails (`quality_failed`).
- **Cold start OK** — you do **not** need a prior `pgjudge` report.
- On FAIL / `AGENT_JUDGE` → apply **`pgjudge`**, fix code/prompts, **re-run the same door**.
- Improve-iter budgets are **agent-owned across CLI reinvokes** (see [Doors](#doors)).
- **LWM note:** gender leading chips (`inanimate:learn-by-heart`,
  `inanimate:suffix-rule-binding`, `animated:fixed-article`) and Places article
  scopes punch via **Leading Word Match**; `inanimate:meaning-changers` uses
  sense-anchor then LWM (see `apps/api/app/pglpl/README.md` LWM scope map).

