<h2 id="howto" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. How to use (Cursor prompts)</h2>

Copy-paste style. Prefer **`@pgbattest`** or the keyword in the message.

**Single scope (most common):**

```text
pgbattest places:cities
pgbattest inanimate:learn-by-heart
```

Agent: run `python ops/local/run_all.py pgbattest --scope places:cities` (or the noun-gender scope). On fail → `pgjudge` → fix → re-invoke until shipped or budget exhaust (then **deferred-live**, continue if more scopes).

**Several scopes:**

```text
pgbattest places:cities, numbers:ordinals, adjectives:endings
pgbattest inanimate:learn-by-heart, animated:animals, plural:plural
```

Agent: `--scopes places:cities,numbers:ordinals,adjectives:endings`; continue after deferred-live; print overall table.

**After a fail (same door again):**

```text
pgjudge
# …fix the issue…
pgbattest places:cities
```

**With continuous implement loop:**

```text
aciub — after each product fix, pgbattest the affected scope until shipped or deferred-live
```

**Stage-end compare (refactor plans):** When a phase finishes paragraph-gen work for
named scopes, run `pgbattest` on **those scopes only**, then print a table:

| Scope | Baseline (locked campaign) | This stage | Delta |

**Locked baseline for LWM / recent Places+Noun campaigns** (≈2026-07-30 evening → 2026-07-31 ~03:00):

| Scope | Baseline outcome | Source artifact |
|-------|------------------|-----------------|
| `places:continents` | 2/2 pass (full-pool×2) | `ops/run-logs/pglpl-wide-fullpool-260730-1128.summary.json` |
| `places:countries` | 2/2 pass | same |
| `places:states` | shipped (Door A+B) | `ops/run-logs/pglpl-phase1-states-retest-260730.json` |
| `places:cities` | shipped | `ops/run-logs/pgbattest-places_cities.json` |
| `places:everyday` | 2/2 pass | wide fullpool summary |
| `inanimate:learn-by-heart` | failed_first5 | `ops/run-logs/pgbattest-inanimate_learn-by-heart.json` |
| `inanimate:suffix-rule-binding` | failed_all | `ops/run-logs/pgbattest-inanimate_suffix-rule-binding.json` |
| `animated:fixed-article` | shipped | `ops/run-logs/pgbattest-animated_fixed-article.json` |
| `inanimate:meaning-changers` | failed_first5 | `ops/run-logs/pgbattest-inanimate_meaning-changers.json` |

Delta labels: `improved` / `same` / `regressed` / `n/a`. Regression from baseline
`shipped` → apply **`pgjudge`** within budgets before closing the stage.

**Ineffective (avoid):**
- Asking for `pgjudge` *before* any live run when starting cold.
- Skipping Door A and jumping to all-pool.
- Abandoning after one fail without a fix attempt while budget remains.

