<h2 id="doors" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Doors and budgets</h2>

| Constant | Default | Meaning |
|----------|--------:|---------|
| `MAX_FIRST_5_WORDS_ITER` | **3** | Max fix→reinvoke cycles for Door A |
| `MAX_ALL_WORDS_ITER` | **3** | Max fix→reinvoke cycles for Door B |

One CLI run = **one attempt** (Door A ×2, then Door B ×1 if A passed, then Door C unless `--no-door-c`).  
Outcome JSON: `shipped` | `shipped_and_verified` | `quality_failed` | `failed_first5` | `failed_all`.  
Exit 0 only when every requested scope is `shipped_and_verified` (or `shipped` with `--no-door-c`).  
After budget exhaust: record **deferred-live** (§4.1-style lay note) and move on.

When appending to [`docs/pglpl/PGBATTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md`](../../../docs/pglpl/PGBATTEST_CATALOG_SCOREBOARD.md) (via **`pgtestcom`** or manual tip), include **run stamp** `YYMMDD-hhmm` (local campaign start) and **wall duration** (`Ns` + `~N min`) on §2 timeline rows — same convention as expgtest summary stamps.

