<h2 id="with-judge" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. With <code>pgjudge</code> (DRY)</h2>

| Rule | Owns |
|------|------|
| **`pgbattest`** | Order, budgets, tables, when to retry |
| **`pgjudge`** | Autopsy of one FAIL / `AGENT_JUDGE` |
| **`pgpbp`** | Paragraph play-by-play for Door **A/B/C** fails on a **recorded** run (`pgpbp-pgbattest-door-c-paragraph-playbyplay.mdc`) |
| **`pgtestcom`** | One `pgbattest` pass + scoreboard tip + vs prior `§6.xx` compare (`pgtestcom-pgbattest-compare-and-scoreboard.mdc`) |

`pgbattest` **calls** `pgjudge` on pipeline fail. `pgjudge` does **not** start campaigns. Door C artifacts land under `ops/run-logs/tmp/pgbattest-door-c-*.json`. After a run is on the scoreboard, **`pgpbp §6.xx`** deep-dives every paragraph that failed Door A, B, or C (produce → verify → gate → punch → judges).

